#para(((emph: "", text: "A Level 1 Wizard with a single spell is entirely predictable: the opponent knows what is coming, saves a dispel die for it, and the model spends the game as an expensive banner. One spell more gives every Wizard a choice to make in each Magic phase, and the lores can carry it — each has three spells at every level, so even a Level 1 Wizard picking two is choosing rather than taking what is left.
